WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:02.502
Now that we're inside of Stever House.

2
00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:06.873
This is our first campus building
to be designated a green building

3
00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.176
with the goal of significantly reducing
the negative impact

4
00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.078
of the building on the environment.

5
00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:16.916
It received a silver rating for leadership
in energy and environmental design.

6
00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:21.087
But right now, we can see
the recreation room in Stever House,

7
00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:25.658
which is home to a variety of activities
for the first year students that live here.

8
00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:29.429
The supplies here include pool equipments,
Ping-Pong paddles

9
00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:32.832
and balls, foosball tables,
as well as a lot of board games.

10
00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:37.570
This is also where the residential hall
kitchen is open to all residents use.

11
00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:38.905
As we mentioned earlier,

12
00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:42.876
our first year students are required
to be on a meal plan, so there's only

13
00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:47.213
typically just one kitchen prep building
in our first year of residence halls.

14
00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.482
In upperclassman housing, however, there's

15
00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:53.219
usually more kitchens per building
where you will have a personal kitchen,

16
00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.121
if you live in an apartment style.

17
00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.791
Creating community here in the residence halls

18
00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:01.795
is another central focus
for all CMU residential staff.

19
00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:05.131
In all campus housing,
we follow a house model

20
00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.534
where each residence
hall has a house fellow.

21
00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:10.904
These are full time professional staff
hired by CMU

22
00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:14.941
that oversee our resident assistants
and community advisors

23
00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:18.878
to provide a vision for daily life
in CMU housing communities.

24
00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:22.615
They usually act as a liaison
to many campus resources,

25
00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.985
including academics,
counseling or health services.

26
00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:30.457
In the middle level support,
we have our community advisors or CAs.

27
00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:35.128
These are usually previously successful
RAs or resident assistants,

28
00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:38.431
and they help to oversee
all current RAs in the building.

29
00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:42.402
And finally, we have resident assistants
located on every floor,

30
00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.605
very similar to other schools but here at CMU,

31
00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:49.075
our RAs really want to get to know
all students a lot better.

32
00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:53.046
So they help to plan house events,
to also help you get to know

33
00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.814
other people living around you.

34
00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.917
They also do live on the floor,
so they are always available

35
00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.720
to answer questions
about campus resources.

36
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.723
There's also an on-call RA
every single night.

37
00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:06.860
So if you have an emergency
or need someone to talk to,

38
00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:09.195
you will always have someone available
for you.

39
00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:14.195
And lastly, you may have seen a lot of
green colors and cacti located in Stever,

40
00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:19.567
and that is because each of our residence
halls have their own house colors and emblems.

